## Routing

```
Route                             Guard          View
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/login                            public         LoginView
/                                 authenticated  DashboardView
/inbox                            authenticated  InboxView
/inbox/:id                        authenticated  NotificationDetailView
/subscriptions                    authenticated  SubscriptionCenterView
/ops/config                       ops_read       OpsConfigView
/ops/config/:id                   ops_read       ConfigDetailView
/dispatch                         dispatch_read  DispatchPanelView
/dispatch/trips/:id               dispatch_read  TripDetailView
/finance                          finance_read   FinanceView  (tab router)
/finance/transactions             finance_read   TransactionsTab
/finance/reconciliation           finance_read   ReconciliationTab
/finance/imports                  finance_read   ImportsTab
/reports                          reports_read   KpiReportsView
/reports/:metric_id               reports_read   MetricDetailView
* (catch-all)                     —              NotFoundView
```

### `src/routes.rs`

```rust
use yew_router::prelude::*;

#[derive(Clone, Routable, PartialEq)]
pub enum Route {
    #[at("/login")]     Login,
    #[at("/")]          Dashboard,
    #[at("/inbox")]     Inbox,
    #[at("/inbox/:id")] InboxDetail { id: String },
    #[at("/subscriptions")] Subscriptions,
    #[at("/ops/config")]    OpsConfig,
    #[at("/ops/config/:id")] OpsConfigDetail { id: String },
    #[at("/dispatch")]      Dispatch,
    #[at("/dispatch/trips/:id")] TripDetail { id: String },
    #[at("/finance")]       Finance,
    #[at("/finance/transactions")] Transactions,
    #[at("/finance/reconciliation")] Reconciliation,
    #[at("/finance/imports")]    Imports,
    #[at("/reports")]       Reports,
    #[at("/reports/:id")]   MetricDetail { id: String },
    #[not_found]
    #[at("/404")]        NotFound,
}
```

### Auth guard pattern

```rust
// components/layout/private_route.rs
#[function_component(PrivateRoute)]
pub fn private_route(props: &PrivateRouteProps) -> Html {
    let auth = use_auth();                       // reads AuthContext
    let navigator = use_navigator().unwrap();

    use_effect_with(auth.token.clone(), move |token| {
        if token.is_none() {
            navigator.push(&Route::Login);
        }
    });

    if auth.token.is_none() {
        html! { <Spinner /> }
    } else if let Some(perm) = &props.require_permission {
        if auth.has_permission(perm) {
            props.children.clone()
        } else {
            html! { <ForbiddenView /> }
        }
    } else {
        props.children.clone()
    }
}
```

---

## State model

State is split into domain slices. Each slice lives in its own `Context` pair (state + dispatch), avoiding re-renders in unrelated subtrees.

```
AppContext  (auth, network, ui)
  ├── NotificationsContext
  ├── OpsContext
  ├── DispatchContext
  ├── FinanceContext
  └── ReportsContext
```

### `src/store/state.rs`

```rust
// ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#[derive(Clone, PartialEq, Default)]
pub struct AuthState {
    pub user_id:  Option<Uuid>,
    pub username: Option<String>,
    pub role:     Option<String>,
    pub token:    Option<String>,      // persisted to sessionStorage
    pub permissions: Vec<String>,
}
impl AuthState {
    pub fn has_permission(&self, p: &str) -> bool {
        self.permissions.iter().any(|x| x == p)
    }
}

// ── Network ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#[derive(Clone, PartialEq, Default)]
pub struct NetworkState {
    pub online:             bool,
    pub pending_sync_count: usize,   // queued mutations not yet replayed
}

// ── UI (transient — never persisted) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#[derive(Clone, PartialEq, Default)]
pub struct UiState {
