## Offline-first design

### Three-layer cache strategy

```
Read path:
  1. Render immediately from store (may be stale)
  2. Fetch from API in background
  3. If fetch succeeds → update store + write to gloo-storage
  4. If fetch fails (offline) → set cache.stale = true, show OfflineBanner

Write path (mutations):
  1. Optimistic update: apply action to store immediately
  2. Try HTTP request
  3a. Success → confirm (possibly reconcile response with optimistic state)
  3b. Failure (network) → enqueue to SyncQueue, show sync indicator
```

### `src/offline/sync_queue.rs`

```rust
/// A mutation waiting to be replayed when the network recovers.
#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]
pub struct QueuedMutation {
    pub id:         Uuid,
    pub method:     String,   // "POST" | "PUT" | "DELETE"
    pub path:       String,
    pub body:       Option<serde_json::Value>,
    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,
}

/// Persisted to IndexedDB under key "sync_queue".
pub struct SyncQueue;

impl SyncQueue {
    pub fn enqueue(m: QueuedMutation) { /* write to IDB */ }
    pub fn drain() -> Vec<QueuedMutation> { /* read + clear IDB */ }
    pub fn len() -> usize { /* count stored items */ }
}
```

